  "question": {
    "text": "In a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CE</mi></math> transistor amplifier, the audio signal voltage across the collector resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, if the base resistance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> and the current amplification of the transistor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> then the input signal voltage is"
